        "original_id": "012ba6fd-727a-5a2e-94ed-c1103050ee0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stuart Pankin, Adrian Lyne, James Dearden\n- Works: Not Necessarily the News, Dinosaurs, Curb Your Enthusiasm, Honey, We Shrunk Ourselves, Arachnophobia, Fatal Attraction\n- Roles: Bob Charles, Earl Sinclair, Ben Heineman, Jimmy\n- Topics: Television acting, film acting, voice acting\n\nFacts:\n- Fatal Attraction is a 1987 American psychological thriller film directed by Adrian Lyne and written by James Dearden.\n- Stuart Pankin played Jimmy in Fatal Attraction.\n- Stuart Pankin appeared in Honey, We Shrunk Ourselves and Arachnophobia.\n- On television, Stuart Pankin played anchor Bob Charles in Not Necessarily the News.\n- On television, Stuart Pankin played Earl Sinclair in Dinosaurs.\n- On television, Stuart Pankin played Orthodox Jew Ben Heineman in Curb Your Enthusiasm.\n- Stuart Pankin also made many guest appearances in television shows and provided voice work for various animated shows and films.",
